        // read without the lock is a snapshot. A process step committing between that read and the
        // write (Resolve moving a ticket out of IN PROCESS) was reverted by a PUT carrying back the
        // status it had read, and the ended flow left the record open with no task. Locked, the step
        // either committed before the checks read the row - and the stale status is refused as any
